# Manual trip receipt email lock

## Canonical rule

Customer trip invoice / receipt email is **manual only**.

Allowed senders:

- Authenticated **customer** for their own completed trip → own auth account email only
- Authenticated **admin/staff** → rider auth email on file only

## Never remove or “simplify away”

- `send-trip-receipt` rejects service-role / cron tokens
- Customer destination must equal `auth.user.email` (no free-typed third party)
- Admin destination must equal the rider auth email on file
- `sendTripInvoiceEmail` requires `assertManualReceiptEmailOpts` (`toEmail` + `sentBy` + `customer_app|admin_panel`)
- Completion / capture / tip-window / sweep store PDF only (`generate_only`) — never email
- `trip-invoice-process` rejects `send_email` / `resend_email`

## Why

Production once accepted any typed destination after trip ownership checks, so a demo / store-review login could email invoice PDFs (fare, addresses) to arbitrary addresses — a privacy leak.

Lock tests: `src/lib/__tests__/manualTripReceiptEmail.test.ts`

## Do not

- Auto-email on trip complete or payment capture
- Fall back to `resolveCustomerEmail` inside the invoice sender
- Select a non-existent `customers.email` column for the recipient gate
- Allow service role to invoke `send-trip-receipt`
